## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/illpixel.html
- Summary (EN): Detects illegal floating-point pixels (NaN and infinite values) in a layer, then fixes them by blending neighbors or zeroing, or flags them with a highlight for shader debugging.
- Résumé (FR) : Détecte les pixels flottants illégaux (NaN et infinis) et les répare ou les signale pour le débogage des shaders.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the original layer that may contain bad values"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Illegal Pixels", "meaning": "method: blend surrounding pixels, zero the pixel, show with highlight, or show by isolating"}, {"name": "Highlight Color", "meaning": "color for flagged pixels in highlight mode"}, {"name": "Detect", "meaning": "NaN values, infinite values, both, or a custom rule"}, {"name": "Rule", "meaning": "custom detection comparing pixels with Less Than, Greater Than, Equal and similar operators"}]

- Caveats: ["Detection works only on 16 and 32 bit float data; integer formats cannot reveal bad pixels.", "Zeroing clears the whole pixel to avoid color shifts; repairing large blocks can produce blurry spots."]

